{"id":"mahabharata-2-062","work":"mahabharata","part":2,"partName":"सभापर्व","partNameEn":"Sabha Parva","unit":62,"title":"द्विषष्टितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 62 · Draupadi's question to the assembly","summary":{"en":"Dragged before the elders, Draupadi laments that no one defends her and demands an answer: was she won or not? Bhishma admits that dharma is subtle and he cannot decide, and says that Yudhishthira himself must answer.","kn":"ಹಿರಿಯರ ಮುಂದೆ ಎಳೆತರಲ್ಪಟ್ಟ ದ್ರೌಪದಿ ಯಾರೂ ತನ್ನನ್ನು ರಕ್ಷಿಸುತ್ತಿಲ್ಲವೆಂದು ವಿಲಪಿಸಿ, ತಾನು ಗೆಲ್ಲಲ್ಪಟ್ಟೆನೇ ಇಲ್ಲವೇ ಎಂದು ಉತ್ತರ ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾಳೆ. ಧರ್ಮ ಸೂಕ್ಷ್ಮ, ತಾನು ನಿರ್ಣಯಿಸಲಾರೆ, ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರನೇ ಉತ್ತರಿಸಬೇಕು ಎಂದು ಭೀಷ್ಮನು ಒಪ್ಪಿಕೊಳ್ಳುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"वृद्धों के सामने घसीटी गई द्रौपदी विलाप करती हैं कि कोई उनकी रक्षा नहीं करता, और उत्तर माँगती हैं: क्या वे जीती गईं या नहीं? भीष्म स्वीकार करते हैं कि धर्म सूक्ष्म है और वे निर्णय नहीं कर सकते, और कहते हैं कि युधिष्ठिर स्वयं उत्तर दें।","te":"పెద్దల ఎదుటకు ఈడ్వబడిన ద్రౌపది ఎవరూ తనను రక్షించడం లేదని విలపించి, తాను గెలవబడ్డానా లేదా అని సమాధానం అడుగుతుంది. ధర్మం సూక్ష్మమైనది, తాను నిర్ణయించలేనని, యుధిష్ఠిరుడే బదులివ్వాలని భీష్ముడు ఒప్పుకుంటాడు.","ta":"பெரியோர் முன் இழுத்து வரப்பட்ட திரௌபதி எவரும் தன்னைக் காக்கவில்லையே என்று புலம்பி, தான் வெல்லப்பட்டேனா இல்லையா என்று பதில் கேட்கிறாள். தர்மம் நுட்பமானது, தம்மால் தீர்மானிக்க முடியாது, யுதிஷ்டிரரே பதில் சொல்ல வேண்டும் என்று பீஷ்மர் ஒப்புக்கொள்கிறார்.","ml":"മുതിർന്നവർക്കു മുന്നിൽ വലിച്ചിഴയ്ക്കപ്പെട്ട ദ്രൗപദി, തന്നെ ആരും സംരക്ഷിക്കുന്നില്ലെന്ന് വിലപിക്കുന്നു; താൻ ജയിക്കപ്പെട്ടതാണോ അല്ലയോ എന്ന ഉത്തരം ആവശ്യപ്പെടുന്നു. ധർമ്മം സൂക്ഷ്മമാണെന്നും തനിക്ക് തീരുമാനിക്കാനാവില്ലെന്നും ഭീഷ്മർ സമ്മതിക്കുന്നു; യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻതന്നെ ഉത്തരം പറയണമെന്ന് അദ്ദേഹം പറയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 2.62; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Wed Apr 19 2006","sections":[{"title":"द्यूतपर्व","titleEn":"Dyuta Parva (The dice game)","verses":[{"text":"द्रौपद्युवाच","meaning":{"en":"Draupadi said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"पुरस्तात्करणीयं मे न कृतं कार्यमुत्तरम् ।\nविह्वलास्मि कृतानेन कर्षता बलिना बलात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"What I should have done first I did not do, and now I am bewildered, dragged by force by this strong man."}},{"n":2,"text":"अभिवादं करोम्येषां गुरूणां कुरुसंसदि ।\nन मे स्यादपराधोऽयं यदिदं न कृतं मया ॥","meaning":{"en":"I salute these elders in the Kuru assembly; let it be no fault of mine that I did not do so earlier."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":3,"text":"सा तेन च समुद्धूता दुःखेन च तपस्विनी ।\nपतिता विललापेदं सभायामतथोचिता ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shaken by him and by grief, that ascetic-like woman, unused to such treatment, fell and lamented in the hall."}},{"text":"द्रौपद्युवाच","meaning":{"en":"Draupadi said:"}},{"n":4,"text":"स्वयंवरे यास्मि नृपैर्दृष्टा रङ्गे समागतैः ।\nन दृष्टपूर्वा चान्यत्र साहमद्य सभां गता ॥","meaning":{"en":"I was seen by kings who gathered in the arena at my svayamvara, and never before anywhere else; today I have come into an assembly."}},{"n":5,"text":"यां न वायुर्न चादित्यो दृष्टवन्तौ पुरा गृहे ।\nसाहमद्य सभामध्ये दृश्यामि कुरुसंसदि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whom neither wind nor sun saw before in the house, I am seen today in the midst of the hall, in the Kuru assembly."}},{"n":6,"text":"यां न मृष्यन्ति वातेन स्पृश्यमानां पुरा गृहे ।\nस्पृश्यमानां सहन्तेऽद्य पाण्डवास्तां दुरात्मना ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whom the Pandavas could not bear to see touched even by the wind in the house, they now put up with being touched by a wicked man."}},{"n":7,"text":"मृष्यन्ते कुरवश्चेमे मन्ये कालस्य पर्ययम् ।\nस्नुषां दुहितरं चैव क्लिश्यमानामनर्हतीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"These Kurus tolerate it that a daughter-in-law and daughter, undeserving, is tormented; I think it is a turn of time."}},{"n":8,"text":"किं त्वतः कृपणं भूयो यदहं स्त्री सती शुभा ।\nसभामध्यं विगाहेऽद्य क्व नु धर्मो महीक्षिताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"What is more wretched than that I, a virtuous, fair woman, enter the midst of the hall today? Where is the dharma of kings?"}},{"n":9,"text":"धर्म्याः स्त्रियः सभां पूर्वं न नयन्तीति नः श्रुतम् ।\nस नष्टः कौरवेयेषु पूर्वो धर्मः सनातनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"We have heard that righteous women were not taken to the assembly in former times; that ancient, eternal dharma is lost among the Kauravas."}},{"n":10,"text":"कथं हि भार्या पाण्डूनां पार्षतस्य स्वसा सती ।\nवासुदेवस्य च सखी पार्थिवानां सभामियाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"How can I, wife of the Pandavas, sister of Dhrishtadyumna, friend of Vasudeva, come to this assembly of kings?"}},{"n":11,"text":"तामिमां धर्मराजस्य भार्यां सदृशवर्णजाम् ।\nब्रूत दासीमदासीं वा तत्करिष्यामि कौरवाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Say whether this wife of the king of dharma, born of equal caste, is a slave or not a slave, Kauravas, and I will do so."}},{"n":12,"text":"अयं हि मां दृढं क्षुद्रः कौरवाणां यशोहरः ।\nक्लिश्नाति नाहं तत्सोढुं चिरं शक्ष्यामि कौरवाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"This base man, destroyer of the Kauravas' fame, torments me hard. I will not be able to bear this long, Kauravas."}},{"n":13,"text":"जितां वाप्यजितां वापि मन्यध्वं वा यथा नृपाः ।\nतथा प्रत्युक्तमिच्छामि तत्करिष्यामि कौरवाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whether you think me won or not won, kings, I want a reply in that way, and I will act accordingly, Kauravas."}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":14,"text":"उक्तवानस्मि कल्याणि धर्मस्य तु परां गतिम् ।\nलोके न शक्यते गन्तुमपि विप्रैर्महात्मभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I have told you, fortunate lady, that the highest course of dharma cannot be fathomed in the world even by great brahmins."}},{"n":15,"text":"बलवांस्तु यथा धर्मं लोके पश्यति पूरुषः ।\nस धर्मो धर्मवेलायां भवत्यभिहितः परैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"How a strong man sees dharma in the world, that becomes the dharma stated by others at the time of dharma."}},{"n":16,"text":"न विवेक्तुं च ते प्रश्नमेतं शक्नोमि निश्चयात् ।\nसूक्ष्मत्वाद्गहनत्वाच्च कार्यस्यास्य च गौरवात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I cannot decide your question with certainty, because of its subtlety, its depth, and the weight of the matter."}},{"n":17,"text":"नूनमन्तः कुलस्यास्य भविता नचिरादिव ।\nतथा हि कुरवः सर्वे लोभमोहपरायणाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Surely the end of this family will come before long, since all the Kurus are given to greed and delusion."}},{"n":18,"text":"कुलेषु जाताः कल्याणि व्यसनाभ्याहता भृशम् ।\nधर्म्यान्मार्गान्न च्यवन्ते यथा नस्त्वं वधूः स्थिता ॥","meaning":{"en":"Though born in families, fortunate lady, and sorely struck by calamity, they do not fall from righteous paths, as you, our daughter-in-law, now stand."}},{"n":19,"text":"उपपन्नं च पाञ्चालि तवेदं वृत्तमीदृशम् ।\nयत्कृच्छ्रमपि संप्राप्ता धर्ममेवान्ववेक्षसे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Such conduct, Panchali, is fitting for you, who even in distress look only to dharma."}},{"n":20,"text":"एते द्रोणादयश्चैव वृद्धा धर्मविदो जनाः ।\nशून्यैः शरीरैस्तिष्ठन्ति गतासव इवानताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"These elders led by Drona, who know dharma, stand with hollow bodies, bowed, as if lifeless."}},{"n":21,"text":"युधिष्ठिरस्तु प्रश्नेऽस्मिन्प्रमाणमिति मे मतिः ।\nअजितां वा जितां वापि स्वयं व्याहर्तुमर्हति ॥","meaning":{"en":"I think Yudhishthira is the authority on this question; he should himself say whether you are won or not."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":22,"text":"तथा तु दृष्ट्वा बहु तत्तदेवं\nरोरूयमाणां कुररीमिवार्ताम् ।\nनोचुर्वचः साध्वथ वाप्यसाधु\nमहीक्षितो धार्तराष्ट्रस्य भीताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing her thus, so many times, crying like a distressed osprey, the kings, afraid of Dhritarashtra's son, said nothing, good or bad."}},{"n":23,"text":"दृष्ट्वा तु तान्पार्थिवपुत्रपौत्रां-\nस्तूष्णींभूतान्धृतराष्ट्रस्य पुत्रः ।\nस्मयन्निवेदं वचनं बभाषे\nपाञ्चालराजस्य सुतां तदानीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing those sons and grandsons of kings silent, Dhritarashtra's son, smiling as it were, spoke to the daughter of the Panchala king."}},{"n":24,"text":"तिष्ठत्वयं प्रश्न उदारसत्त्वे\nभीमेऽर्जुने सहदेवे तथैव ।\nपत्यौ च ते नकुले याज्ञसेनि\nवदन्त्वेते वचनं त्वत्प्रसूतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Let this question rest, noble lady, on Bhima, Arjuna, Sahadeva and Nakula, and your husband; let them speak a word that comes from you."}},{"n":25,"text":"अनीश्वरं विब्रुवन्त्वार्यमध्ये\nयुधिष्ठिरं तव पाञ्चालि हेतोः ।\nकुर्वन्तु सर्वे चानृतं धर्मराजं\nपाञ्चालि त्वं मोक्ष्यसे दासभावात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Let them say in the midst of the nobles that Yudhishthira is not master, because of you, Panchali; let all of them call the king of dharma a liar, and you will be freed from slavery."}},{"n":26,"text":"धर्मे स्थितो धर्मराजो महात्मा\nस्वयं चेदं कथयत्विन्द्रकल्पः ।\nईशो वा ते यद्यनीशोऽथ वैष\nवाक्यादस्य क्षिप्रमेकं भजस्व ॥","meaning":{"en":"Let the great-souled king of dharma, who stands in dharma and is like Indra, say it himself: whether he was your master or not; by his word, take one of them quickly."}},{"n":27,"text":"सर्वे हीमे कौरवेयाः सभायां\nदुःखान्तरे वर्तमानास्तवैव ।\nन विब्रुवन्त्यार्यसत्त्वा यथाव-\nत्पतींश्च ते समवेक्ष्याल्पभाग्यान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"For all these Kauravas in the assembly, in the midst of their distress, are suffering for you; noble in nature, they do not speak properly, looking at your unfortunate husbands."}},{"n":28,"text":"ततः सभ्याः कुरुराजस्य तत्र\nवाक्यं सर्वे प्रशशंसुस्तदोच्चैः ।\nचेलावेधांश्चापि चक्रुर्नदन्तो\nहा हेत्यासीदपि चैवात्र नादः ।\nसर्वे चासन्पार्थिवाः प्रीतिमन्तः\nकुरुश्रेष्ठं धार्मिकं पूजयन्तः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the assembly all praised the Kuru king's words loudly; they waved their garments, shouting and crying Ha! Ha!, and all the kings were pleased, honoring that righteous best of the Kurus."}},{"n":29,"text":"युधिष्ठिरं च ते सर्वे समुदैक्षन्त पार्थिवाः ।\nकिं नु वक्ष्यति धर्मज्ञ इति साचीकृताननाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"All the kings looked at Yudhishthira, their faces turned aside, wondering, What will the knower of dharma say?"}},{"n":30,"text":"किं नु वक्ष्यति बीभत्सुरजितो युधि पाण्डवः ।\nभीमसेनो यमौ चेति भृशं कौतूहलान्विताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"They were very curious what Bibhatsu, Bhimasena and the twins, unconquered in battle, would say."}},{"n":31,"text":"तस्मिन्नुपरते शब्दे भीमसेनोऽब्रवीदिदम् ।\nप्रगृह्य विपुलं वृत्तं भुजं चन्दनरूषितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When that noise stopped, Bhimasena, raising his big, round, sandal-smeared arm, said this."}},{"n":32,"text":"यद्येष गुरुरस्माकं धर्मराजो युधिष्ठिरः ।\nन प्रभुः स्यात्कुलस्यास्य न वयं मर्षयेमहि ॥","meaning":{"en":"If this Yudhishthira, king of dharma, our elder, were not lord of this family, we would not tolerate this."}},{"n":33,"text":"ईशो नः पुण्यतपसां प्राणानामपि चेश्वरः ।\nमन्यते जितमात्मानं यद्येष विजिता वयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He is master of our merits and austerities and even of our lives. If he thinks himself won, then we are won."}},{"n":34,"text":"न हि मुच्येत जीवन्मे पदा भूमिमुपस्पृशन् ।\nमर्त्यधर्मा परामृश्य पाञ्चाल्या मूर्धजानिमान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"No mortal who touched these hairs of Panchali could escape from me alive, touching earth with his feet."}},{"n":35,"text":"पश्यध्वमायतौ वृत्तौ भुजौ मे परिघाविव ।\nनैतयोरन्तरं प्राप्य मुच्येतापि शतक्रतुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Look at my two long, rounded arms like iron bars; once caught between them even Indra could not escape."}},{"n":36,"text":"धर्मपाशसितस्त्वेवं नाधिगच्छामि संकटम् ।\nगौरवेण निरुद्धश्च निग्रहादर्जुनस्य च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bound by the noose of dharma, I do not seek a way out of this trouble, held back by respect and by Arjuna's restraint."}},{"n":37,"text":"धर्मराजनिसृष्टस्तु सिंहः क्षुद्रमृगानिव ।\nधार्तराष्ट्रानिमान्पापान्निष्पिषेयं तलासिभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"But if released by the king of dharma, I would crush these sinful Dhartarashtras with the palm of my hand, like a lion crushing little deer."}},{"n":38,"text":"तमुवाच तदा भीष्मो द्रोणो विदुर एव च ।\nक्षम्यतामेवमित्येवं सर्वं संभवति त्वयि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Bhishma, Drona and Vidura said to him: Be patient; everything is possible in you."}}]}]}